From ee504baeec1c1e14b1f3b6ea4e1a5eaec5d5e377 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:18:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1] serial: qcom-geni: fix line allocation without serial
 aliases
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

of_alias_get_highest_id() returns -ENODEV when the DT has no "serial"
aliases at all. The non-console path then passes max_alias_num + 1 as
the lower bound to ida_alloc_range(), which rejects negative bounds, so
every non-console GENI UART fails to probe with "Invalid line -19".
Seen on the Samsung Galaxy A52 (SM7125), whose Bluetooth UART never
bound. Treat "no aliases" as -1 so allocation starts at line 0.

Fixes: a53be6945f51 ("serial: qcom-geni: Remove alias dependency from qcom serial driver")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
index 3633723acef8..7e55f27942c1 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -289,6 +289,10 @@ static struct qcom_geni_serial_port *get_port_from_line(int line, bool console,
 	} else {
 		int max_alias_num = of_alias_get_highest_id("serial");
 
+		/* no serial aliases at all: allocate from line 0 */
+		if (max_alias_num < 0)
+			max_alias_num = -1;
+
 		if (line < 0 || line >= nr_ports)
 			line = ida_alloc_range(&port_ida, max_alias_num + 1,
 					       nr_ports - 1, GFP_KERNEL);
-- 
2.55.0

